ONEDRAFT
CAD-AI — Aria Powered
Job & Worker Execution System
Version 1.0
Status: Implementation Specification
Architecture: Distributed Asynchronous Execution
Queue: PostgreSQL-backed MVP / Redis-compatible production interface
Workers: API / Model / Geometry / Compliance / Validation / Documentation / Export
Identifiers: UUID
Execution Model: Durable Jobs + Queued Tasks + Worker Claims + State Transitions
AI Layer: Aria Powered

1. EXECUTION DESIGN PRINCIPLE
OneDraft requires a durable execution layer between the Runtime Orchestrator and the computational subsystems.
The Runtime Orchestrator determines:
what must happen
The Job & Worker Execution System determines:
when, where, and under what execution conditions it happens
The workers perform:
the actual computation
The resulting architecture is:
CLIENT
 ↓
API
 ↓
RUNTIME ORCHESTRATOR
 ↓
JOB SYSTEM
 ↓
QUEUE
 ↓
WORKER
 ↓
DOMAIN SERVICE
 ↓
RESULT
 ↓
VALIDATION
 ↓
PROJECT MODEL
The Job & Worker Execution System therefore becomes the execution backbone of OneDraft.

2. CORE EXECUTION PRINCIPLE
No expensive computational operation shall execute directly inside the synchronous API request lifecycle.
Operations such as:
geometry generation
model regeneration
compliance analysis
validation
drawing generation
sheet composition
document generation
PDF export
package hashing
large-scale model reconstruction
redline resolution
shall execute through durable jobs.
The API returns a job_id.
The client may subsequently inspect job state through the API.

3. JOB LIFECYCLE
The universal job lifecycle is:
CREATED
 ↓
QUEUED
 ↓
CLAIMED
 ↓
RUNNING
 ↓
VALIDATING
 ↓
COMPLETED
Alternative terminal states are:
FAILED
CANCELLED
EXPIRED
INVALIDATED
A job shall never transition backward from a terminal state.

