57. QUEUE ADAPTER
The application shall define an abstract queue interface.
Conceptually:
QueueAdapter
    enqueue()
    claim()
    acknowledge()
    reject()
    retry()
    cancel()
The domain system must not depend directly on a particular queue implementation.

58. MVP QUEUE IMPLEMENTATION
The MVP may use PostgreSQL as the durable queue mechanism.
The implementation may use:
FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
for job claiming.
This minimizes infrastructure requirements during initial development.

59. PRODUCTION QUEUE IMPLEMENTATION
The architecture shall permit migration to a dedicated queue system such as:
Redis
RabbitMQ
NATS
Kafka
without changing the OneDraft domain contracts.
The queue adapter provides the abstraction boundary.

60. QUEUE DURABILITY
A queued job must survive:
API restart
worker restart
application restart
machine restart
The job record is therefore persisted independently of the worker process.

61. ORCHESTRATOR / WORKER SEPARATION
The Runtime Orchestrator does not perform computational work directly.
It creates:
job graph
and delegates execution to workers.
Example:
RUNTIME ORCHESTRATOR

create MODEL_COMMAND job
create GEOMETRY_GENERATION dependency
create VALIDATION_RUN dependency
create DRAWING_GENERATION dependency
create DOCUMENT_GENERATION dependency
Workers then execute the graph.

62. EVENT-DRIVEN CONTINUATION
Job completion may trigger downstream jobs.
Example:
GEOMETRY_GENERATION
        ↓
GEOMETRY_COMPLETED
        ↓
VALIDATION_RUN CREATED
Similarly:
VALIDATION_COMPLETED
        ↓
DRAWING_GENERATION CREATED
And:
DRAWING_GENERATION COMPLETED
        ↓
DOCUMENT_GENERATION CREATED
The Runtime Orchestrator remains responsible for determining whether the next stage is valid.

63. FAILURE PROPAGATION
If a required upstream job fails:
UPSTREAM FAILED
 ↓
DEPENDENT JOBS
 ↓
BLOCKED
Blocked jobs shall not execute against incomplete prerequisites.
They may be marked:
CANCELLED
or:
INVALIDATED
according to orchestration policy.

64. VALIDATION GATE
Certain downstream operations require successful validation.
For example:
VALIDATION
 ↓
DOCUMENT GENERATION
The document generation job shall verify that the required validation state exists before proceeding.
This prevents generation of a final package from an unvalidated model state.

65. FINAL PACKAGE GATE
Final document packaging requires:
model state valid
geometry state valid
required drawings complete
required validation complete
code manifest identified
document artifacts complete
Only then may:
DOCUMENT_HASH
and:
PACKAGE_VERIFICATION
execute.

66. ACCEPTANCE GATE
Customer acceptance occurs only after:
PACKAGE_VERIFICATION = PASSED
The acceptance subsystem records:
project_id
revision_id
model_version_id
document_package_id
code_manifest_id
validation_run_id
customer_id
accepted_at

67. AUDIT INTEGRATION
Every significant execution event shall integrate with:
